---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// The app's page. Linked from inside the app, from the App Store listing as
// both the support and marketing URL, and from anywhere Brett points people.
// Indexed, unlike the policy pages, because this is the one that has to be
// findable.
const appStore = 'https://apps.apple.com/app/id6808987732';
---

<Base
  title="Slumbio · Sleep sound, made as it plays"
  description="An iPhone sleep app. Thirty-five sounds, and most of them are generated as they play, so they never repeat."
  puck={false}
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">iPhone</p>
    <h1>Slumbio</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sound that is made as it plays, breathing you can see, and one button
      from the couch to the sleep timer.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="body">
    <p>
      Most sleep apps play a recording on a loop. Given long enough you start
      hearing the seam, and once you have heard it you cannot stop hearing it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Slumbio has thirty-five sounds and thirty-three of them are built as
      they play, from noise and filters, one frame at a time. Rain that never
      falls the same way twice. A fire that crackles when it feels like it.
      Wind that gusts and settles on its own schedule. There is no loop,
      because there is no recording to loop. Two of the sounds are
      pre-rendered files and those two do repeat; they are labelled.
    </p>
    <p>
      Layer up to six at once. Each has a level and two controls that reach
      into the sound itself, so a light rain becomes a downpour and a room
      becomes a bigger room.
    </p>

    <figure class="shots">
      <img src="/slumbio/shot-tonight.webp" width="420" height="913"
           alt="The Tonight screen: a mix called Long Rain, a play button, the wind-down routine and a note on sleep." loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/slumbio/shot-sounds.webp" width="420" height="913"
           alt="The Sounds screen: two sounds playing and layered, with the rest of the library below." loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/slumbio/shot-breathe.webp" width="420" height="913"
           alt="The Breathe screen: six breathing patterns and a session length." loading="lazy" />
    </figure>

    <h2>Breathing you can see</h2>
    <p>
      A soft body of light sits behind every screen. In a breathing session it
      is the instruction: the screen fills on the inhale and empties on the
      exhale, with a tap at each turn and a breath sound underneath. Six
      patterns, two to fifteen minutes, and a session always ends at the end of
      a cycle rather than mid-breath.
    </p>

    <h2>Nothing leaves the phone</h2>
    <p>
      No account, no server, no analytics, no tracking. There is no network
      code in the app at all, which is why the App Store privacy label reads
      Data Not Collected. The sleep journal, the mixes and the settings live on
      the device and nowhere else.
    </p>

    <h2>Free, and meant to stay usable</h2>
    <p>
      Twelve sounds, two layers, two breathing patterns, the sleep timer,
      bedside mode and every note are free for good. Plus adds the rest.
    </p>

    <p class="cta">
      <a href={appStore}>Get Slumbio on the App Store</a>
    </p>

    <p class="fine">
      Something wrong, or an idea? Write to
      <a href="mailto:brettmboggs@gmail.com">brettmboggs@gmail.com</a>. I read
      all of it.
    </p>

    <ul class="links">
      <li><a href="/slumbio/privacy/">Privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/slumbio/terms/">Terms</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <a class="back-link" href="/">&larr; Home</a>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .body h2 {
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .cta {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .fine {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .shots {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .shots img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(51, 41, 28, 0.18);
  }
  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .shots {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
    .shots img:last-child {
      display: none;
    }
  }
  .links {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
